---
import CompareLayout from "../../layouts/CompareLayout.astro";
import { aiExposure } from "../../data/page-answers.ts";
import { SFI, VERIFIED } from "../../data/compare.ts";
---

<CompareLayout
  name="Hubbl"
  title="sf-intelligence vs Hubbl: Org Audits Compared"
  description="Hubbl scores and benchmarks your Salesforce org as a hosted service. sf-intelligence answers one question at a time, free and on your laptop. Compare them."
  path="/compare/hubbl"
  heading="sf-intelligence vs Hubbl"
  lede="Hubbl calls itself “the Intelligence Layer for Salesforce”, the same phrase this project uses. The products are different shapes: Hubbl scans an org and hands back a scored, benchmarked fix list. sf-intelligence answers a specific question when you ask it."
  short="Hubbl is a hosted service that scans your org, benchmarks it against other orgs and keeps monitoring it. Its first assessment is free; paid plans aren’t priced publicly. sf-intelligence is free, runs on your computer and answers one question at a time, naming every component. Pick Hubbl for a scored report leadership will read; pick sf-intelligence before you change a specific thing."
  rows={[
    { label: "What it is", sfi: SFI.what, them: "A hosted service that scans an org, scores it and recommends fixes. A second product line covers business processes" },
    { label: "What you get", sfi: "An answer to the question you asked, with each component named", them: "A prioritized fix list, benchmarked against other orgs, with a live readout from a partner" },
    { label: "Where metadata is processed", sfi: SFI.where, them: "In Hubbl’s service. The assessment needs no install" },
    { label: "Price", sfi: SFI.price, them: "Assessment $0. Professional is “priced as a share of your Salesforce spend”; Enterprise is custom. Hubbl says it doesn’t price by seat or by org" },
    { label: "MCP", sfi: "It is an MCP server", them: "“API &amp; Hubbl MCP access” is listed on the Enterprise plan" },
    { label: "Benchmarks against other orgs", sfi: "No. It only knows your org", them: "Yes, “against thousands of orgs”" },
    { label: "Ongoing monitoring", sfi: "No. You refresh the snapshot when you want", them: "Scheduled scans and monitoring on Professional" },
    { label: "Source code", sfi: SFI.source, them: "Closed" },
  ]}
  chooseSfi={[
    "To know <strong>what breaks</strong> before you change one field, flow or permission",
    "Answers <strong>inside your AI assistant</strong>, every day, at no cost",
    "Org metadata that <strong>stays on your computer</strong>",
    "A tool that <strong>can’t write</strong> to the org at all",
  ]}
  chooseThem={[
    "A <strong>scored health report</strong> to put in front of leadership",
    "To see how your org <strong>compares with other orgs</strong>",
    "Scheduled scans and a trend over time, with nothing to refresh by hand",
    "Process discovery across your Salesforce workflows",
  ]}
  notSfi={[
    "You want a benchmark against other companies’ orgs. sf-intelligence only knows yours",
    "You want a dashboard or report for people who won’t use an AI assistant. There is no web app",
    "You want the org watched continuously. The snapshot is as current as your last refresh",
  ]}
  example={aiExposure}
  exampleIntro="A question from the AI-readiness side, asked of Verdant, the demo org that ships inside sf-intelligence."
  sources={[
    { label: "hubbl.com pricing", href: "https://www.hubbl.com/pricing" },
    { label: "hubbl.com home page", href: "https://www.hubbl.com/" },
  ]}
  verified={VERIFIED}
  faqs={[
    {
      q: "Is sf-intelligence the same as Hubbl’s Intelligence Layer?",
      a: "No. They share a phrase, not a product. Hubbl is a commercial hosted service. sf-intelligence is a free, source-available tool you run yourself, with no connection to Hubbl.",
    },
    {
      q: "Does Hubbl have an MCP server?",
      a: "Yes. Hubbl’s pricing page lists “API &amp; Hubbl MCP access” on its Enterprise plan. So being reachable from an AI assistant no longer separates the two; price, where the metadata goes and the shape of the answer do.",
    },
    {
      q: "How much does Hubbl cost?",
      a: "The guided org assessment is $0. Professional is priced as a share of your Salesforce spend and Enterprise is custom; neither price is published. An earlier version of this page said Hubbl priced per org; its pricing page now says it doesn’t price by seat or by org.",
    },
    {
      q: "Can I use both?",
      a: "Yes, and they fit together. Use a scan to find cleanup candidates across the org, then ask sf-intelligence what depends on each one before you remove it. See <a href=\"/use-cases/what-breaks-if-you-delete-a-field\">what breaks if you delete a field</a>.",
    },
  ]}
  related={[{ href: "/use-cases/agent-readiness-audit", label: "Agent-readiness audit with sf-intelligence" }]}
>
  <h2>A scan versus a question</h2>
  <p>Hubbl’s unit of work is a scan. You connect the org, it reviews packages, automation, fields, code and permissions, and you get a ranked list of what to fix, compared with other orgs. Run it again later and you have a trend.</p>
  <p>sf-intelligence’s unit of work is a question. There’s no score and no dashboard. You ask “can I delete this field?” or “who can edit Amount on Invoice?” and the answer names the components it found and what it couldn’t check. A scan tells you where to look across the org; a question tells you what is true about the one thing you are about to change.</p>
</CompareLayout>
